# Credentials — never committed, in a public repo least of all.
# Keep keys OUTSIDE the repo where possible; a .gitignore entry does not stop `git add -f`,
# an editor sync, a backup tool, or a `docker build` context from picking one up.
# GCP service-account keys are named <project>-<12 hex>.json. Match the SHAPE, not each
# project, so a key for a project nobody has thought of yet is still ignored on arrival.
*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f].json
*service-account*.json
*-credentials*.json
*-key.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
.env
.env.*

# collected events — never committed
data/

# validation run output — evidence is regenerated, not versioned
validation/output/*
!validation/output/.gitkeep

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# node (snippet minification only)
node_modules/

# os / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Credential filenames the hyphen-prefixed patterns above do NOT match. `credentials.json` is the
# literal name of Google's OAuth client download, and `key.json` is what
# `gcloud iam service-accounts keys create` writes by default -- the two most likely credential
# files to appear in a repo, and both were unignored until 2026-07-28. This repo is public.
credentials.json
credentials-*.json
client_secret*.json
*service_account*.json
*_service_account*.json
key.json
*key.json
application_default_credentials.json
*secret*.json
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.p8

# Internal development record — kept on disk, deliberately not tracked.
# The public tree carries what a user or contributor needs; how each slice was scoped and every
# trap found along the way is working material. Read them locally, don't commit them.
error.md
docs/spec-increment-*.md
